# {{ project_name }} — product as code

Your product is defined as a typed, validated graph under [`{{ product_dir }}/`]({{ product_dir }}/),
and generated into [`{{ output_bundle }}`]({{ output_bundle }}) by
[FastPDLC](https://github.com/tarvitave/fastpdlc).

## Workflow

```bash
pip install fastpdlc=={{ fastpdlc_version }}

fastpdlc validate      # schema + references + staleness — this is the CI gate
fastpdlc build         # regenerate {{ output_bundle }} after editing an artifact
```

Commit `{{ output_bundle }}` alongside your edits; the `product-validate` workflow
fails any PR where it has drifted out of sync with `{{ product_dir }}/`.

## Adding artifacts

Each file under `{{ product_dir }}/<type>/` is one record. Its `id` must start with
the type's prefix and match the filename (e.g. `{{ product_dir }}/terms/TERM-payment.md`
has `id: TERM-payment`). Reference fields must resolve to a real id — see
[`product.config.yaml`](product.config.yaml) for the types this repo defines.
